Pass only if all of these are true:
- The slide teaches or explains the concept clearly.
- The slide does not ask the student to perform an action the slide cannot support.
- The slide does not contain activity directions such as click, tap, drag, move, choose, point, count, circle, draw, write, or similar commands.
- The visible text, attached image, and lesson concept all agree.
- If the text depends on a pictured group, count, left/right comparison, or visual arrangement, the image must exist and support it exactly.
- The image does not add new facts that contradict the slide text.

Fail if you are unsure.

